    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make a flash pizza with homemade pizza dough that will be ready to top and bake in less than 10 minutes without using any yeast or waiting for it to rise. He uses self-rising flour, white sugar, freshly grated Parmesan, plain Greek-style yogurt, and a little bit of olive oil. He mixes them until they form a shaggy dough, kneads it for about 3-4 minutes, and rolls it out thinly. The dough will be enough for two pizzas and can be shaped according to one's preference. ",
